-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1784517078151317001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"696b05fd-aa56-4713-bc2f-67f5da725dc2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"839b-f6d2-7e1a-4051"}],"description":"## Idea (parking lot — out of scope for the code-health analyzer epic 839b-f6d2)\nAdd a polyglot **dependency-graph** capability to the code-health analyzer (module/file coupling, fan-in/fan-out, cycles) so a per-project graph signal can feed the metrics registry.\n\n## Why it's a separate idea, not part of the epic\nThe portability audit found there is **no mature, single, drop-in polyglot dependency-graph OSS CLI** (unlike LOC/complexity/duplication, which scc/lizard/jscpd cover). Realistic paths, all heavier:\n- Per-language adapters behind the analyzer seam: dependency-cruiser / madge (JS/TS), pydeps (Python), `go mod graph` (Go), jdeps (Java).\n- Polyglot foundations to build on (frameworks, not turnkey): tree-sitter + GitHub stack-graphs, or Sourcegraph SCIP indexers; heavyweight end: CodeQL.\n\n## Open questions (to design before promoting out of idea)\n- Which graph signals are worth a metric (cycle count? max coupling? fan-in hotspots?) and are they cross-language comparable?\n- Single polyglot foundation (tree-sitter/SCIP) vs. a registry of per-language adapters with honest Unavailable where none exists?\n- Cost/determinism/CI-time budget vs. value.\n\nTreat as future work; do not block the scc/lizard/jscpd epic on it.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","839b-f6d2-7e1a-4051"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"95a267a5-f29a-4140-99fb-0e755a8803bd","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"idea","tags":["metrics","code-health","idea"],"ticket_id":"7e17-d75e-dfa2-4055","ticket_type":"story","title":"Polyglot dependency-graph analyzer capability for code-health metrics","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2eb20529-c852-47ed-a2a3-ca400ccfb0f4","95a267a5-f29a-4140-99fb-0e755a8803bd","696b05fd-aa56-4713-bc2f-67f5da725dc2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659626131769001,"uuid":"fb9087c7-06a7-46ee-92d6-ae5b43022329"}